    "recommendations": "Ensuring that the single access point and extended driveway remain clear of obstructions at all times could significantly improve emergency vehicle approach and reduce response delays. Maintaining adequate driveway width and surface conditions along the full length of the approach would support heavier emergency apparatus maneuvering. Clearly marking the primary access point from the main road may assist responding units in locating the entry quickly, particularly under low-visibility conditions. Where the unpaved trail extends toward the rear of the property, keeping that route passable could provide an alternate path for responder movement and staging, partially offsetting the limited rear access identified on the property."
